    "d94b5d55-eb15-4cf4-80d0-eaa6ad65a4fc": {
      "type": "content-list",
      "blocks": {
        "template--16177341137065__d94b5d55-eb15-4cf4-80d0-eaa6ad65a4fc-image-3": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "apply_overlay": false,
            "devices": "mobile_desktop",
            "content_position": "underLeft",
            "subheading": "",
            "title": "",
            "description": "<p><strong>You’ve shared so many chapters together since then. What are some of the little things that have come to define your relationship?</strong></p><p></p><p>Being together for almost ten years means we’ve really grown up alongside one another. We’ve navigated so many different seasons of life together, and I think one of the things that defines our relationship is continuing to make the choice to choose one another through all of them.</p><p>Communication has always been incredibly important to us and something we continue to prioritise. But I also think adventure has become such a big part of who we are together.</p><p>With Guy being a photographer, we’ve been fortunate enough to travel to places I could once only have dreamed of. The adventures we’ve shared and the memories we’ve made around the world are something I’ll forever be grateful for. Guy has opened my world in so many ways, and experiencing all of it alongside him has made it even more special.</p><p><br/></p><p><br/></p><p></p><p><strong>Uluwatu has always held a special place in your relationship. What made returning there for this moment feel so meaningful?</strong></p><p>Uluwatu, and particularly Uluwatu Surf Villas, holds such a special place in our hearts. It’s somewhere we’ve returned to year after year and a place that has become woven into our relationship.</p><p>We’ve made some of our most treasured memories there, met some of our now closest friends and crossed paths with so many incredible people. There’s something about being there that allows us to slow down, come back to ourselves and connect even more deeply with one another.</p><p>It already held so much meaning for us, so for Guy to choose that exact place to propose made the moment feel almost surreal. I had dreamed about being asked there, which made discovering that he had chosen it himself even more special.</p>",
            "description_mobile": "<p><strong>You’ve shared so many chapters together since then. What are some of the little things that have come to define your relationship?</strong></p><p></p><p>Being together for almost ten years means we’ve really grown up alongside one another. We’ve navigated so many different seasons of life together, and I think one of the things that defines our relationship is continuing to make the choice to choose one another through all of them.</p><p>Communication has always been incredibly important to us and something we continue to prioritise. But I also think adventure has become such a big part of who we are together.</p><p>With Guy being a photographer, we’ve been fortunate enough to travel to places I could once only have dreamed of. The adventures we’ve shared and the memories we’ve made around the world are something I’ll forever be grateful for. Guy has opened my world in so many ways, and experiencing all of it alongside him has made it even more special.</p><p><br/></p><p><br/></p><p></p><p><strong>Uluwatu has always held a special place in your relationship. What made returning there for this moment feel so meaningful?</strong></p><p>Uluwatu, and particularly Uluwatu Surf Villas, holds such a special place in our hearts. It’s somewhere we’ve returned to year after year and a place that has become woven into our relationship.</p><p>We’ve made some of our most treasured memories there, met some of our now closest friends and crossed paths with so many incredible people. There’s something about being there that allows us to slow down, come back to ourselves and connect even more deeply with one another.</p><p>It already held so much meaning for us, so for Guy to choose that exact place to propose made the moment feel almost surreal. I had dreamed about being asked there, which made discovering that he had chosen it himself even more special.</p>",
            "colour_style": "dark",
