            "description": "<p><strong>Guy went through the NMJ Bespoke process to create your ring. Which details feel most like you?</strong></p><p>There are so many details I love.</p><p>The 2ct elongated cushion-cut centre stone was such a beautiful choice. I adore its proportions and the way it catches the light — I genuinely can’t stop looking at it. The shape also suits my hand so beautifully.</p><p>I had always dreamed of a three-stone design because of what it represents: our past, our present and our future. After almost ten years together, that symbolism feels particularly special. </p><p>We already have so much history behind us, but there is still so much ahead of us too.</p><p>The trillion-cut side stones are another detail I absolutely love. They give the ring something a little unexpected and distinctive while still feeling timeless. Everything about the proportions and design feels so considered, and knowing Guy went through the Bespoke process to bring it all together makes it even more meaningful.</p><p>It feels perfectly mine.<br/><br/></p><p><br/></p><p><strong>Take us back to the proposal itself. What do you remember most clearly from that moment overlooking the ocean?</strong></p><p>The proposal itself is honestly a beautiful blur.</p><p>I had <strong>absolutely no idea</strong> it was coming, which still makes me laugh because I always thought I’d somehow know. I was convinced I’d pick up on a tiny clue or sense that Guy was acting differently, but there was nothing.</p><p>Because Guy is a photographer, taking photos together is such a normal part of our lives. So when he suggested we take one overlooking the ocean, I didn’t think anything of it.</p><p>Then I turned around.</p><p>I saw his hand move towards his back pocket and watched him drop to one knee, and I think I went into complete shock. All I could say was, <em>“No, you’re not. No, you’re not!”</em> because I genuinely couldn’t believe it was happening — especially in the exact spot where I had secretly dreamed he might one day propose.</p><p>And somehow, there was still another surprise waiting. Guy had organised for my best friend to fly over and join us, which made an already overwhelming moment even more special.</p><p>We then had another six days in Uluwatu to celebrate our engagement, surrounded by a place and people we love. It was absolute magic.</p><p>I’ve been on cloud nine ever since.</p>",
